  "content": "API list-endpoint convention: every collection response is wrapped in {\"items\": [...]} — never a bare JSON array. Reasons: CSRF/JSON-hijacking historical risk, and the envelope leaves room for pagination metadata without breaking clients later. Server side uses the writeList[T] helper in internal/handlers/json.go (coerces nil slices to [] so clients never see \"items\": null). Frontend uses requestList(schema, path) in lib/api.ts which unwraps before returning — components still get plain arrays. Endpoints covered: /api/projects, /api/memories, /api/stats/events, /api/usage/by-day, /api/usage/summary. /api/graph stays {nodes, links} because it's already an object.\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003ctags\u003e[\"api\", \"convention\", \"security\"]\u003c/tags\u003e",
  "tags": [
    "api",
    "convention",
    "security"
  ],
